# Rank 1560 / CVE-2025-32947: PeerTube's ActivityPub collection crawler
# incremented its loop counter only at the bottom of the loop body, so a
# branch that continued past it never advanced the budget and the crawl
# looped forever (loop with unreachable exit, CWE-835; the advisory:
# infinite loop in the AP crawler). crawlCollectionPage in
# server/core/lib/activitypub/crawl.ts ran `while (nextLink && i < limit)
# { if (typeof nextLink === 'string') { const remoteHost = new
# URL(nextLink).host; if (remoteHost === WEBSERVER.HOST) continue; ... } ...
# nextLink = body.next; i++; ... }` -- the don't-crawl-ourselves `continue`
# jumps back to the condition without executing the i++ further down, so a
# hostile collection whose next link stays on the instance's own host spins
# the loop with i frozen below limit. Commit 76226d8568 ("Fix infinite loop
# in AP crawl") moves the increment to the top of the loop body (`while
# (nextLink && i < limit) { i++; ... }`) so every iteration advances the
# budget whatever branch it takes.
#
# Detection is the structural loop-restart fact: a while, do-while or
# update-less for(;;) loop whose body carries a `continue` dominated by no
# progress step for the variables the loop's exit reads -- no assignment,
# augmented assignment or update writing one, no method call receiving one
# as its receiver, and no call to a closure defined in the same function
# whose body carries such evidence -- re-tests an unchanged exit and takes
# the same branch forever. Evidence counts only where it dominates the
# restart, so a sibling branch's progress step never covers a restart that
# branch does not execute. VYQL-DOS-050 (code.LoopRestartWithoutProgressCheck)
# reports it and stays quiet on the benign forms: the top-increment fix, a
# condition that assigns (`while ((line = read()) != null)`), which
# advances every iteration; a loop with no body progress whose exit is
# external; a receiver advance before the restart; a restart covered
# through a closure the same function defines (`getArg()` shifting the
# argument vector the condition reads); and a restart whose dominating path
# carries a call the fact cannot interpret -- an import, a parameter, or a
# callback whose body advances the exit -- which is neutralised in data by
# the rule's `unless` over core.LoopProgressCallSideEffect, not suppressed
# in the frontend.

test "rank1560: the self-host continue skips the loop's only progress"
  lang javascript
  file server/core/lib/activitypub/crawl.ts
  expect VYQL-DOS-050
  code
  ```
  const WEBSERVER = { HOST: 'example.com' };
  const ACTIVITY_PUB = { FETCH_PAGE_LIMIT: 100 };

  async function crawlCollectionPage(argUrl, handler) {
    let url = argUrl;

    const response = await fetchAP(url);
    const firstBody = response.body;

    const limit = ACTIVITY_PUB.FETCH_PAGE_LIMIT;
    let i = 0;
    let nextLink = firstBody.first;
    while (nextLink && i < limit) {
      let body;

      if (typeof nextLink === 'string') {
        const remoteHost = new URL(nextLink).host;
        if (remoteHost === WEBSERVER.HOST) continue

        url = nextLink;

        const res = await fetchAP(url);
        body = res.body;
      } else {
        body = nextLink;
      }

      nextLink = body.next
      i++
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1560: the fixed revision advances the budget before any branch"
  lang javascript
  file server/core/lib/activitypub/crawl.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-050
  code
  ```
  const WEBSERVER = { HOST: 'example.com' };
  const ACTIVITY_PUB = { FETCH_PAGE_LIMIT: 100 };

  async function crawlCollectionPage(argUrl, handler) {
    let url = argUrl;

    const response = await fetchAP(url);
    const firstBody = response.body;

    const limit = ACTIVITY_PUB.FETCH_PAGE_LIMIT;
    let i = 0;
    let nextLink = firstBody.first;
    while (nextLink && i < limit) {
      i++

      let body;

      if (typeof nextLink === 'string') {
        const remoteHost = new URL(nextLink).host;
        if (remoteHost === WEBSERVER.HOST) continue

        url = nextLink;

        const res = await fetchAP(url);
        body = res.body;
      } else {
        body = nextLink;
      }

      nextLink = body.next
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1560: a condition that assigns advances on every iteration"
  lang javascript
  file server/core/lib/activitypub/crawl.ts
  reject VYQL-DOS-050
  code
  ```
  async function crawlLines(path, handler) {
    const reader = openReader(path);

    let line;
    let i = 0;
    while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null && i < 100) {
      if (line.isEmpty()) continue

      await handler(line)
      i++
    }
  }
  ```

